const secondaryRows = [
 ['The Salt Quarry: Closed Shift','Salt Quarry','snow','courtyard','rout','apothecary:5',34,'Alden Marr','A quarry insurer has sealed the mine with its workers inside. Alden asks the crew to trace a voice heard through its flooded lift.','The report calls it a beast. I know the person who is trying to answer us.','The lift opens. The foreman’s log shows that a failed bond was moved into the lowest shaft.','m035',[]],
 ['The Salt Quarry: Broken Ramp','Salt Quarry','snow','ridge','rout','bogcolossus:2,broker:2,apothecary:1',35,'Orren Pike','A shattered loading ramp divides the rescue route. Bonded carriers and armed insurers still defend the machinery.','The ramp can carry us if we spread our weight. Do not give those beasts a single narrow line.','The lower ramp is secure. A surviving worker gives Alden a signal from his partner.','m061',[]],
 ['The Salt Quarry: Blue Seam','Salt Quarry','snow','islands','rout','brinedrake:2,tuskling:1,apothecary:2',36,'Alden Marr','Cold water pours through a blue mineral seam. Its guardians have trapped the last work crew beside a disabled winch.','Nara left marks here. She knew we would follow, even in this form.','The workers leave through the winch shaft. Below, something is forcing Nara to keep the water still.','m062',[]],
 ['The Salt Quarry: A Voice of Her Own','Salt Quarry','crypt','bridge','rescue','oathfiend:1,inkwitch:3,rootward:2',37,'Nara Marr','A living bond pins Nara’s river form inside the last shaft. Protect her while the crew breaks the machinery around it.','I am still here. Ask me before you touch the seal.','Nara is free and chooses to travel with Alden. A recovered maintenance frame also accepts the crew’s invitation.','m063',['alden','nara','ballast']],
 ['The Honest Manifest','Rookmarket','village','steps','rescue','broker:1,pugilist:1,longbow:3,cantor:1',35,'Lark Pell','A freight runner has stolen proof that relief shipments were sold abroad. The owners call for guards before the cargo can be unloaded.','If they want to call me a thief, let them first explain whose food this is.','Lark delivers the cargo and joins the crew. His signed manifests make a better introduction than his stories.','m037',['lark']],
 ['The Listening Foundry','Lumen Foundry','ruins','steps','boss','dredgeframe:1,reedrunner:3,mirehydra:2',45,'Ilyra Senn','A dormant foundry holds the tool that can release Nara’s borrowed form. Its sentry mistakes every request for a repair order.','This machine has never heard the word no. We must stop it before we can teach it.','The sentry rests. Nara chooses her human shape again and keeps the river’s strength as her own.','m064',[]],
 ['A Traveler at the Lantern Market','Lantern Market','village','courtyard','rescue','broker:3,pugilist:1,recruit:2',44,'Sol Ansel','A traveler from the outer coast protects a market vendor from debt collectors. Their damaged memory leaves them unable to hold the street alone.','I know how to hold a blade. I do not know why this place feels like a warning.','Sol accepts a place aboard the clinic boat. Orren offers to repair their blade without demanding a story in return.','m066',['sol']],
 ['The Beacon in the Ash','Ash Beacon','volcano','ridge','reach','cinderpod:2,brinedrake:1,marshcat:2',45,'Orren Pike','Sol’s blade needs an old beacon core found above a cooling lava field. Reach the housing while its guardians close the slope.','The core is on the high platform. Bring it back before the rock loses its heat.','The blade is repaired. Sol remembers a departure by choice, and chooses to remain with the crew.','m067',[]],
 ['The Oath of the Empty Coat','Stillwater Dock','harbor','courtyard','rout','twinblade:1,pugilist:1,warden:2,recruit:2',49,'Sera Kest','Deserters use the city guard’s coats to seize food from the same dock Sera once defended. She must decide what remains of their oath.','Put down the coats if you will not carry what they promise. The kitchens need hands more than prisoners.','The surviving deserters surrender their weapons and work under the dock council’s watch.','m054',[]],
 ['The Case of the Borrowed Heir','Highlock','fort','bridge','boss','relicblade:1,twinblade:2,longbow:2,timekeeper:1',50,'Alden Marr','A former colleague claims the right to renew Nara’s expired bond. He waits at the old keeper’s gate with a second contract hidden beneath the first.','A person cannot be inherited. Not through a title, and not through a debt.','The second contract fails as the first did. Alden follows the claim to the office that manufactured it.','m066',[]],
 ['The Court of One','Highlock','cathedral','courtyard','boss','cantor:1,twinblade:2,relicblade:2,medium:2',51,'Nara Marr','A new keeper has made himself judge, creditor, and witness. He turns his failing claim into a river beast rather than accept Nara’s refusal.','You never asked for my answer. Hear it now: this bond is ended.','The private court dissolves. Nara and Alden give its archives to the public hearing, including the claims against other families.','m070',[]]
];
